# Atrium

Two founders selling **agent-run automation** to firms of 100–1000 people. CRUD is cheap. They sell **outcomes on channels the client already uses**. Follow the industry’s wake (n8n credentials, UiPath assets, LangGraph assistants + bindings). Do the small wedges they do not: GraphRAG not dumpster RAG, two-level client taxonomy, human gates, folder/email/Telegram. Do not invent 280 fake employees.

## Oficio → instance → binding (translate founder ideas before coding)

| They say | Build | Do not build |
|---|---|---|
| A job (file, parse, notify) | One **oficio** in the catalog | A new species per vertical |
| E&P vs Aircraft vs another client | Same oficio, new **instance** + utility assembly | “Aircraft Taxonomist” as a different job |
| Mailbox, API, bot token | Named **credential binding** on the instance | A Custodian agent; secrets in Graph JSON; one global `.env` forever |
| Knobs (folder, cadence, tree) | Fields on that instance `config` | A Configurator product |
| Smart scheduler someday | Orchestrator + per-instance cadence **now** | Replace LangGraph with if-else |

Reuse the specialist if the job already belongs to them (Parser parses; Courier notifies; Mailroom connects). Split only when the job is genuinely different.

## When they name a utility

1. Name the oficio (one job). Instance it per client if needed.
2. Tool handler in `apps/api/app/runtime/tools.py`.
3. Seed tool + agent + assignment + Orchestrator route in `apps/api/app/db/seed.py`.
4. Admin → Graph shows the node/edge. Ask Scribe to sync the roster.
5. Workspace/Admin is chrome. Screens do not own the work.

## Non-negotiables

- New capability = **agent + tool + catalog + graph edge**. Not a Python function with a button.
- Humans see the same graph as the model (Admin → Graph).
- No second chatbot, CRM, website builder, or extra control plane.
- Mid-market line: intake → parse → classify → GraphRAG and/or SQL → human review → notify.
- GraphRAG (Neo4j + Qdrant), not vector-only. No Chroma.
- Local Ollama. Do not block Watchman on the 32b model.
- Channels are agents (Watchman, Mailroom, Courier), not an integrations page.
- Secrets stay off the graph. Scribe owns `AGENTS.md` roster markers.

## When lost

Read `AGENTS.md`, then `docs/HOW_IT_WORKS.md`. If it is not an oficio, an instance, a binding, a tool, or the graph those agents share, it is the wrong change.
